  ONE TOOL CAVEAT surfaced here: maven-module-deps.sh's section [3] treats
  every javax.* name as JDK-shipped unless it matches the explicitly-removed
  list (annotation/xml.bind/activation/jws/xml.ws/transaction) — javax.help
  was never JDK-shipped at all (it is, and always was, the standalone jhall
  library), so section [3] would have silently swallowed it as noise had it
  ever appeared there. It didn't: section [1]'s unfiltered import scan
  already reports `import javax.help` etc. directly, so nothing was actually
  missed here — noted for whichever future module hits this gap without
  section [1]'s help.

  THE TWO ROSETTA JARS, VERIFIED PER-CLASS (same method as modules/
  console/pom.xml, which needs the identical pair): `unzip -l thirdparty/
